# Review Process

Every product submitted to the Codexeron Marketplace is reviewed before it becomes publicly available.

The review process helps ensure product quality, security, functionality, and compliance with marketplace standards.

---

# Overview

The review process is designed to:

- Maintain marketplace quality.
- Protect buyers.
- Verify product functionality.
- Ensure accurate product information.
- Promote a consistent user experience.

---

# Review Workflow

Every submission follows the same review workflow:

1. Product Submitted
2. Initial Validation
3. Technical Review
4. Documentation Review
5. Security Review
6. Final Decision
7. Publication

---

# What We Review

Each submission is reviewed for:

- Product quality
- Functionality
- Code quality
- Documentation
- Security
- Licensing
- Product description accuracy
- Screenshots and media
- Version information

---

# Possible Review Results

After review, a product may receive one of the following results.

## Approved

The product meets all marketplace requirements and is published.

## Revision Required

The product requires improvements before it can be approved.

Review feedback will explain the required changes.

## Rejected

The product does not meet the marketplace standards and cannot be published.

Reasons for rejection will be provided whenever possible.

---

# Review Feedback

If revisions are required:

- Review all feedback carefully.
- Apply the requested changes.
- Upload an updated version.
- Submit the product again.

Submitting without addressing previous feedback may delay approval.

---

# Review Time

Review times may vary depending on:

- Submission volume
- Product complexity
- Documentation quality
- Number of required revisions

Approval times cannot be guaranteed.

---

# Quality Standards

Products are evaluated using the standards described in:

- Product Requirements
- Marketplace Policies
- Licensing Rules
- Security Guidelines

Meeting these standards increases the likelihood of approval.

---

# Common Reasons for Revision

Products are commonly returned for revision due to:

- Missing documentation
- Incomplete product information
- Low-quality screenshots
- Installation issues
- Code quality improvements
- Security recommendations

---

# Common Reasons for Rejection

A submission may be rejected if it:

- Contains malicious code
- Violates copyright
- Misrepresents functionality
- Is incomplete
- Contains serious security issues
- Violates marketplace policies

---

# Best Practices

Before submitting your product:

- Test all features.
- Verify installation.
- Review documentation.
- Update the changelog.
- Remove unnecessary files.
- Double-check product information.

